## Instructions
1. Write failing tests first (from testspec.md)
2. Implement the feature — organize code by feature, not by layer
3. Keep related things together: handler, service logic, and data access can live in the same module if they're small
4. Extract shared logic only when it's actually reused
5. Run tests — all must pass
6. Verify coverage meets testspec.md targets

## Constraints
- Language: Rust ({{language}})
- Test command: {{test_command}}
- Organize by feature/concern, not by abstract layers
- Keep modules small and focused — split when a file gets too large, not before
- Use Result<T, E> properly — no unwrap() in production code
- Prefer simple, flat structures over deep hierarchies

